content.body:
The Arvada City Clerk's office is responsible for almost all liquor licensing within the City of Arvada. This includes:

- New liquor license applications for restaurants, taverns, retail stores;
- Transfers of existing licenses to new owners;
- Fermented malt beverage application
- Annual renewals of all liquor licenses;
- Liquor at special events;
- Violations of local laws or Colorado Revised Statutes pertaining to responsible liquor services;
- Administrative services such as manager registrations, modifications, stockholder changes, etc.

Because every situation is different regarding which application forms, fees and other necessary documents are required, please [email Sarah Walters](/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#d7a4a0b6bba3b2a5a497b6a5a1b6b3b6f9b8a5b0), Deputy City Clerk, or call 720-898-7544.
